        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "The shared propionate-cluster preparation produced both Ce-{24} and Ce-{38}. A mixture of pyridine, water, and propionic acid was added to cerium(IV) ammonium nitrate and ammonium iodide in a glass vial and stirred at 500 rpm for 30 min. Acetonitrile was added, and the mixture stood undisturbed at 20 °C for several weeks. Ce-{24} crystals were identified by single-crystal unit-cell measurements and manually separated from Ce-{38} crystals.",
